[
    {
        "content": "<p>ilyas-mallah edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788\">PR #14788</a>.</p>",
        "id": 632386600,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792187232
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ilyas-mallah <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788#issuecomment-6225333658\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788\">PR #14788</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Panic makes sense to me (perhaps a debug assertion? this can't happen without a bug in cranelift-codegen, so I'm not sure how much benefit there is to unconditionally checking it). And I think the check could be done inside the loop that processes the relocations right before applying them instead of iterating a second time.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Made it a panic, checked in the relocation loop right before each write. I kept it in release builds because the offsets don't only come from cranelift-codegen. DataDescription::write_data_addr and define_function_bytes take them from the caller in safe code, so a debug assertion would still let a release build write past a definition. It's one compare per relocation.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632386832,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792187317
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> ilyas-mallah submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788#pullrequestreview-5554087837\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 632386862,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792187326
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> ilyas-mallah created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788#discussion_r4299676699\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Done, it's now Reloc::patched_len with an exhaustive match, so a new relocation kind won't compile until it states its width.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632386863,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792187326
    },
