    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> ilyas-mallah submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788#pullrequestreview-5557539569\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 632529065,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792235870
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> ilyas-mallah created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788#discussion_r4302472785\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Good catch. <code>patched_len</code> now returns 12 for <code>ElfX86_64TlsGd</code>, covering the <code>lea</code> displacement and the <code>call</code> after it, and the out-of-bounds test has a case for it.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632529066,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792235871
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ilyas-mallah updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788\">PR #14788</a>.</p>",
        "id": 633487543,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792544335
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> ilyas-mallah submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788#pullrequestreview-5593675312\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 633487555,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792544341
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> ilyas-mallah created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14788#discussion_r4331942729\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I also reworded the patched_len doc, which claimed to cover the whole instruction: it counts from the offset to the end of what a linker may rewrite, so the lea bytes before the displacement aren't included. The other TLS relocations each sit on the one instruction a linker rewrites, so their widths stay as they were.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 633487557,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792544341
    },
